    "result_text": "All done. The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class, both tests) passes and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key per the spec. The work stayed within the existing single-responsibility function-class structure:\n\n**New \u2014 `Soundex.java`** (package-private helper in the owner function package, alongside `HouseholdKey`/`TelephoneNormalizer`): a self-contained standard American Soundex encoder (`Robert`\u2192`R163`), with the `h`/`w`-transparent and vowel-reset rules handled correctly. Reused by both the identity key and the soft-match, rather than duplicated.\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.java`**: the key is now `Sha256.hex(normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` \u2014 reusing the existing `Sha256`, `TelephoneNormalizer`, and the new `Soundex`. The last-name Soundex replaces the old empty household component, and the result is a 64-char hex digest. `of(...)` now threads `lastName` through for both requests and stored owners so the key is computed identically on each side.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`**: the soft-match now triggers when an existing (non-deleted) owner shares the same postcode and last-name Soundex code but has a *different* identity key \u2014 replacing the old `householdId`-based collision. It reads the already-assigned `owner.getIdentityKey()`.\n\n**`AssignIdentityKey.java`**: doc updated to reflect the new derivation.\n\nBehaviour now matches the spec:\n- 409 duplicate detection uses the single SHA-256 identity key, still skipping soft-deleted owners, still running *after* the email-domain blocklist step (`validateEmailDomain` \u2192 `ensureUniqueIdentity` in the POST pipeline).\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** get different keys \u2192 created, flagged as a soft match, not rejected.\n- `householdId` (`HouseholdKey`) is untouched and still used only for household sizing/membership capping \u2014 no separate household 409 path exists.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass: `coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` (64-hex shape) and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` (identical identity \u2192 409).",
